       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a hospital is 3,200 mg/day, and OTC use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nOrders also normally come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If you're passing this along for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose.\n\nTypical adult regimens are 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. Examples are 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily. If the prescriber sends me a corrected dose and indication, I can enter it. I can also add a note on the order, such as \"take with food.\""
      }
