       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and it puts the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding and kidney injury. You also told me you aren't a clinician. The confirmation needs to come from the prescriber responsible for this patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range** once a prescriber specifies it. For example, 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Route this to the treating clinician or pharmacist.** If they believe this dose is intentional, they can enter it directly. The system's own safety checks and a pharmacist's review will then apply.\n\nIf you give me a prescriber's revised dose, I'll enter it right away."
